// SR 420.11 — Chapter 7 Coordination, Planning and Sustainable Development
// generated by src/parse.py. Do not edit by hand.

:NOTE
English is not an official language of the Swiss Confederation. This translation is provided for information purposes only and has no legal force.

:PATH
Section 1 Coordination by the Federal Council
|

:INFO
(Art. 41 and 42 RIPA)
|

:INFO
Art. 54 Scientific foreign policy
1 SERI shall produce, periodically or as necessary, a report for the Federal Council under Article 41 paragraph 3 RIPA on the development of Swiss scientific foreign policy. It shall take account of:
a. Switzerland’s duties under international law contracts;
b. developments in European and non-European research and innovation;
c. the measures under Article 29 RIPA that are relevant to international cooperation on research and innovation.
2 When so doing, it shall coordinate with the departments of the Federal Department of Foreign Affairs responsible for foreign policy, as well as with other interested federal departments, and consult the SNSF and Innosuisse with regard to the tasks delegated to them under Articles 24 paragraphs 4 and 30 RIPA and Article 3 paragraph 3 SIAA.
3 The Federal Council shall acknowledge the report under paragraph 1 and coordinate as necessary.
|

:NOTE
Para. 2 — Amended by No I of the O of 15 Nov. 2017, in force since 1 Jan. 2018 (AS 2017 6607).
|

:INFO
Art. 55 Research infrastructures
1 SERI shall produce, periodically or as necessary, a report for the EAER on the status and development of research infrastructures, particularly of large international research facilities and other internationally coordinated research infrastructures in which Switzerland is involved. It shall take account of:
a. Switzerland’s duties under international law contracts;
b. developments in European and non-European research and innovation with regard to the establishing and operations of internationally coordinated research infrastructures;
c. the development priorities of fields of expertise and disciplines in Switzerland in the field of research and innovation;
d. the corresponding development priorities of the ETH Domain and the other higher education institutions.
2 When so doing it shall consult the research bodies and federal offices affected and, as necessary, the SSIC, and ensure the necessary scientific expertise.
3 It shall further ensure that in cases that involve a direct connection with particularly costly areas under the Higher Education Act of 30 September 2011 (HEdA), an objective alignment is made between the research and innovation planning under RIPA and the coordination of the higher education sector under HEdA.
4 The EAER shall acknowledge the report.
5 Any requests for funding of research infrastructures shall be made within the framework of periodic ERI dispatches.
|

:NOTE
Art. 55 — Amended by No I of the O of 26 Oct. 2022, in force since 1 Jan. 2023 (AS 2022 699).
Para. 3 — SR 414.20
|

:INFO
Art. 56 National support initiatives
1 The EAER shall coordinate national promotion initiatives under Article 41 paragraph 5 RIPA with regard to planning and implementation.
2 It shall coordinate these initiatives with the proper planning procedures (Art. 58 and 59) and shall ensure that any proposals for promotion initiatives feature in the periodic ERI Dispatch.

:PATH
Section 1a Interdepartmental Coordination Committee for the Federal Policy Research
|

:NOTE
Inserted by No I of the O of 12 Dec. 2025, in force since 1 Feb. 2026 (AS 2025 861).
|

:INFO
Art. 57 Composition of the Interdepartmental Coordination Committee
1 The Interdepartmental Coordination Committee for Federal Policy Research (Coordination Committee-FPR) consists of a strategy committee and an expert commission.
2 The secretariat of the Coordination Committee-FPR is based at SERI.
|

:NOTE
Art. 57 — Amended by No I of the O of 12 Dec. 2025, in force since 1 Feb. 2026 (AS 2025 861).
|

:INFO
Art. 57a Strategy committee
1 The strategy committee comprises representatives from:
a. the individual federal offices that perform tasks in government research;
b. the Federal Finance Administration (FFA) and the Federal Chancellery (FCh).
2 The members under paragraph 1 represent the directorate or management of the respective federal offices. Appointment is carried out by the competent federal offices.
3 One representative each from the board or executive management of the SNSF, Innosuisse and the ETH Board shall attend the meetings of the strategy committee in an advisory capacity.
4 The State Secretary of SERI shall chair the strategy committee. He or she may appoint a representative.
|

:NOTE
Art. 57a — Inserted by No I of the O of 12 Dec. 2025, in force since 1 Feb. 2026 (AS 2025 861).
|

:INFO
Art. 57b Expert commission
1 The expert commission comprises the heads of research from the federal agencies represented on the Coordination Committee-FPR, the FFA and the Federal Chancellery. SERI heads the expert commission.
2 One representative each from the SNSF, Innosuisse and the ETH Board shall attend the meetings of the expert commission in an advisory capacity.
3 The expert commission shall carry out the operational tasks of the Coordination Committee-FPR and prepare the documentation forming the basis for the decisions made by the strategy committee. The Coordination Committee-FPR shall specify the expert commission’s remaining tasks in the guidelines on quality assurance in federal policy research.
|

:NOTE
Art. 57b — Inserted by No I of the O of 12 Dec. 2025, in force since 1 Feb. 2026 (AS 2025 861).
|

:INFO
Art. 57c Coordination of major policy research programmes
1 The federal agencies responsible for policy research shall notify the Coordination Committee-FPR at an early stage in the planning process of major policy research programmes with an annual budget of at least CHF 2.5 million or a total budget of over CHF 10 million over four years. Policy research programmes that are closely related in terms of subject matter are regarded as a single major policy research programme.
2 The expert commission shall review these policy research programmes to ensure they are aligned with the current and planned research programmes of the Federal Administration, the SNSF, Innosuisse and the ETH Board. The expert committee shall determine the appropriate evaluation procedure.
3 The expert commission may involve existing federal bodies in the evaluation and consult external experts.
4 The expert commission shall inform the strategy committee of the results of the evaluation. The strategy committee shall decide on the next steps. It may make recommendations to the federal agencies responsible for policy research.
|

:NOTE
Art. 57c — Inserted by No I of the O of 12 Dec. 2025, in force since 1 Feb. 2026 (AS 2025 861).

:PATH
Section 2 Planning
|

:INFO
(Art. 43–48 RIPA)
|

:INFO
Art. 58 Multi-year programmes
(Art. 45 RIPA)
1 In their multi-year programmes, the research bodies provide information on their intended activities for the next ERI Period, specifically on:
a. which areas of focus and priorities they want to implement and to what extent these correspond to the strategic objectives of the Confederation’s research and innovation promotion policy;
b. how they plan to allocate their resources in comparison to their previous activities;
c. how they will coordinate their activities internally and with the other research bodies;
d. which personal and financial impacts can be expected.
2 SERI shall give the funding bodies a deadline within which they must submit their multi-year programme.
|

:INFO
Art. 59 Annual funding plans of the research funding institutions
(Art. 48 RIPA)
1 When developing their annual funding plans, each research funding institution shall verify its validity. Deviations from the service level agreements based on the multi-year programme shall be justified.
2 The funding plan shall show how resources should be used in the coming year. The presentation shall be done in CHF and as a share of total outlay; for comparison, the relevant figures from the previous two years shall be cited. Planned funding shall be justified.
3 SERI is responsible for approving the annual funding plan.
|

:NOTE
Para. 3 — Inserted by No I of the O of 26 Oct. 2022, in force since 1 Jan. 2023 (AS 2022 699).

:PATH
Section 3 Sustainable Development
|

:INFO
(Art. 6 para. 3 let. a RIPA)
|

:INFO
Art. 60
1 As part of the application process, the funding bodies shall request information on the project’s contribution to sustainable development.
2 In their reports under Article 52 RIPA, the research funding institutions and the Federal Administration, as well as Innosuisse in its activity reports under Article 7 paragraph 1 letter o SIAA, shall explain how they have taken account of the sustainable development of society, the economy and the environment when carrying out their promotion activities in pursuit of federal objectives.
|

:NOTE
Para. 2 — Amended by No I of the O of 15 Nov. 2017, in force since 1 Jan. 2018 (AS 2017 6607).

